    {
      "id": "MEv6pHsOTkMh9O7BiGsD_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2399.2333577473964,
      "y": 144122.66666666663,
      "width": 2791.800048828125,
      "height": 990,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "NevH_Kr3EljXm6iAi-pRd"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0zM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 321523590,
      "version": 45,
      "versionNonce": 989471814,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785414706472,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "[student@workstation monitoring-drift]$ curl -s \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer ${TOKEN}\" \\\n-X POST ${TRUSTY_ROUTE}/metrics/drift/meanshift \\\n-H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n-d '{\n  \"modelId\": \"diabetes\",\n  \"referenceTag\": \"TRAINING\"\n}' | jq -r '.specificDefinition'\n\nMeanShift gives the per-column probability that the data values seen in a test dataset \ncome from the same distribution of a training dataset, under the assumption that the values are normally distributed.\n\n  - Column            BloodPressure has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column DiabetesPedigreeFunction has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                  Glucose has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                 Diabetes has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column            SkinThickness has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                  Insulin has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column              Pregnancies has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                      Age has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                      BMI has p=0.568817 probability of coming from the training distribution. p >  0.050000\n  - Column              No Diabetes has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "[student@workstation monitoring-drift]$ curl -s \\\n-H \"Authorization: Bearer ${TOKEN}\" \\\n-X POST ${TRUSTY_ROUTE}/metrics/drift/meanshift \\\n-H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n-d '{\n  \"modelId\": \"diabetes\",\n  \"referenceTag\": \"TRAINING\"\n}' | jq -r '.specificDefinition'\n\nMeanShift gives the per-column probability that the data values seen in a test dataset \ncome from the same distribution of a training dataset, under the assumption that the values are normally distributed.\n\n  - Column            BloodPressure has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column DiabetesPedigreeFunction has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                  Glucose has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                 Diabetes has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column            SkinThickness has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                  Insulin has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column              Pregnancies has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                      Age has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]\n  - Column                      BMI has p=0.568817 probability of coming from the training distribution. p >  0.050000\n  - Column              No Diabetes has p=0.000000 probability of coming from the training distribution. p <= 0.050000 -> [SIGNIFICANT DRIFT]",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
